  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA/AFRICOM Workshop 01-25: &quot;Transnational Threats and the Growing International Illicit Crime&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The workshop continues to build on an 8-year NESA-AFRICOM-WJPC series that focuses on smarter border/entry management; creative organizational changes/initiatives to build a short-medium-long term approaches to surveillance; and developing protocols to exchange information/intel more seamlessly between countries and across borders, oceans and continents. This year we have expanded our focus to the Indian Ocean and South Asia to examine four themes: technology; environmental/climate; transnational illicit networks; and maritime security with an aim to build better cooperation regionally and continentally with burden sharing proposals, best practices and leveraging existing training and initiatives..Under Chatham House rule of non-attribution, the event is designed to provide a venue for USAFRICOM, senior security professionals, and young security experts from Africa and Central/Latin America to discuss how best to collaborate between &quot;whole of governments&quot; and &quot;whole of societies&quot; in developing requirements, protocols, processes and policies to address/brainstorm required institutional, organizational, and cultural changes.</narrative>
  </description>
